created: 2025-05-16, last updated: 2026-03-25, [Read more](https://www.answeroverflow.com/m/1372823775669780480)

:wave: ---------------------- Yes, there are a couple of approaches you can use to create a Tenant record during user signup in Wasp.
Option 1: Custom Signup Action The most flexible approach is to create a custom signup action where you have full control over the signup process:
```
...
createUser,
} from 'wasp/server/auth'
export const signup = async (args, { entities: { User, Tenant } }) => {
ensureValidUsername(args)
ensurePasswordIsPresent(args)
ensureValidPassword(args)
try {
// Create the tenant first
const tenant = await Tenant.create({
data: {
name: args.companyName
}
})
const providerId = createProviderId('username', args.username)
const providerData = await sanitizeAndSerializeProviderData({
hashedPassword: args.password,
})
// Create user and link to tenant
await createUser(
providerId,
providerData,
{
tenantId: tenant.id
},
)
} catch (e) {
return {
success: false,
message: e.message,
}
}
return {
success: true,
message: 'User created successfully',
}
```

